<!--
  Colorblind Mode palette, day appearance.

  Day is a LIGHT surface, so every ink here is dark. The app's real
  surfaces are translucent glass over a gradient, so the ratios below are
  measured against the blended composite, not against either layer alone.

  GENERATED by .plans/tools/gen_colorblind_res.py; the ratio in each comment is
  the measured WCAG contrast against #D0D8E4 (L 0.6812), which is the worst-case
  surface of this appearance, namely the darker of the two day surfaces and the
  the two night surfaces. Do not hand-edit a value here without re-running that
  script: the floors are the whole point, and an eyeballed tweak is how a tier
  silently drops below its floor.

  Structure is per (type x strength) for the focus family and per type for
  everything else, because the focus fill is what the user's strength setting
  scales and the semantic colours are what the user's *deficiency* remaps. The
  two axes are independent, so a 9x semantic matrix would be nine copies of
  three colours.
-->
<resources>
